<title>USA: Raytheon CFO sees single-digit dilution.</title>
<headline>Raytheon CFO sees single-digit dilution.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Chief Financial Officer Peter D'Angelo on Thursday that the company would experience earnings dilution &quot;in the high single digits&quot; in 1997 as a result of the Hughes Electronics Corp transaction and the company's planned acquisition of Texas Instruments Inc's defense electronics business.</p>
<p>Raytheon earlier said the Hughes transaction would be minimally accretive in 1998 and increasingly accretive in future years.</p>
<p>((-- Robin Sidel, New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
